    "message": "Port ordered GGUF streaming split and merge tools\n\nAdd a bounded native Rust llama-gguf-split executable and ordered borrowed\nheader writing. Match frozen source split/merge layout, metadata ordering,\nargument quirks, dry runs and retained input ownership, with checked errors\nfor source assertions and undefined parser cases. Begin destructive cleanup\nonly after complete output flush and sync; document later partial cleanup.\n\nValidate unchanged 648 execution inputs on Windows and GNU, 460/464 tests\nper ordinary profile, nine explicit pretrained comparisons per host, and\nCLI plus HTTP/SSE behavior. Check 465 fixture declarations and 103 native\ntool cases per profile with 12,179,168 exact post-operation file bytes.\nRetain original captures, failed checks and same-input continuations.\nArbitrary-byte strings and noncanonical booleans remain a separate open\ncompatibility boundary. All twelve full-port release gates remain open.",
